window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-yukimura-teruhiko"]=[{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v3-p42-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ike-kanji kouenji-rokusuke yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  the no points hardliner  and the day he folds joins the toilet fight uninvited  sliding his glasses up   it s not as though i don t understand the girls  desire to have a temporary toilet  however  i m not convinced that we ought to arbitrarily spend our points  i d like to at least make a decision after collecting a majority vote  the line the chapter keeps against him   even money can move based purely on instinct  i hate that women argue so emotionally    and shinohara s  huh  is the only response printed  loses the toilet vote to hirata s arithmetic    fine  in that case  let s install one toilet    described as beaten   yukimura  who couldn t bear being stared at in silence  broke  folds again when ike sides with hirata s 120 point plan   yukimura still appeared reluctant  but seeing ike join with hirata made him fold  the outburst at the retirement    kouenji  you jerk  what the hell were you thinking     the normally silent yukimura shouted and kicked the ground","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v3-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the no-points hardliner, and the day he folds<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.42–43, p.50–51, p.90, p.98<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Joins the toilet fight uninvited, sliding his glasses up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s not as though I don’t understand the girls’ desire to have a temporary toilet. However, I’m not convinced that we ought to arbitrarily spend our points… I’d like to at least make a decision after collecting a majority vote.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The line the chapter keeps against him: “Even money can move based purely on instinct. I hate that women argue so emotionally.” — and Shinohara&#x27;s &quot;Huh?&quot; is the only response printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Loses the toilet vote to Hirata&#x27;s arithmetic — &quot;Fine. In that case, let’s install one toilet.&quot; — described as beaten: &quot;Yukimura, who couldn’t bear being stared at in silence, broke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Folds again when Ike sides with Hirata&#x27;s 120-point plan: &quot;Yukimura still appeared reluctant, but seeing Ike join with Hirata made him fold.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The outburst at the retirement — &quot;Kouenji, you jerk! What the hell…were you thinking?!&quot; — &quot;The normally silent Yukimura shouted and kicked the ground.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p24-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  the roommate heading named as one of the two roommates ayanokoji means to head back to  he wouldn t return to his room just yet   he d head back to where hirata and yukimura  his other roommates  would be  a hallway question confirms the roommates  ayanokoji with hirata  kouenji  and yukimura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the roommate heading<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.24, p.26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the two roommates Ayanokōji means to head back to.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He wouldn’t return to his room just yet — he’d head back to where Hirata and Yukimura, his other roommates, would be.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A hallway question confirms the roommates: Ayanokōji with Hirata, Kouenji, and Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  2 3  odd company  first quarrel seated at mashima s table with the professor  first to spot that the gathering is odd   this is rather odd  isn t it  ayanokouji   how about you shut up and try listening  the test is probably going to start soon  if they dock our points because you keep blabbing  are you gonna take responsibility   even back on the deserted island  you dragged us all down  can you try not to cause any more problems  first to lose patience with karuizawa  point anxious and practical  trades insults with her under the teacher s eye  paired oddly at the table  by the narrator s note","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32, p.36<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Seated at Mashima’s table with the Professor; first to spot that the gathering is odd.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“This is rather odd, isn’t it? Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about you shut up and try listening? The test is probably going to start soon. If they dock our points because you keep blabbing, are you gonna take responsibility?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even back on the deserted island, you dragged us all down. Can you try not to cause any more problems?”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> First to lose patience with Karuizawa; point-anxious and practical.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Trades insults with her under the teacher’s eye.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Paired oddly at the table, by the narrator’s note.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the roommate heading<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the seat and the roll call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p33-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  2 3  the seat and the roll call sits beside ayanokoji at mashima sensei s table as the zodiac group fills  ayanokoji silently takes the seat next to yukimura  kushida asks why yukimura kun and these other guys are here  mashima sensei rolls the group  sotomura  yukimura  ayanokouji  and karuizawa  from class d  he and the professor stay silent through karuizawa s complaining   how seriously they took the test is left open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the seat and the roll call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.33–35<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits beside Ayanokōji at Mashima-sensei’s table as the zodiac group fills.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji silently takes the seat next to Yukimura; Kushida asks why Yukimura-kun and these other guys are here.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Mashima-sensei rolls the group: Sotomura, Yukimura, Ayanokouji, and Karuizawa, from Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He and the Professor stay silent through Karuizawa’s complaining — how seriously they took the test is left open.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: odd company, first quarrel<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  2 3  the quarrel at the table spends the briefing trading barbs with karuizawa and absorbing mashima s rebuke  snorted derisively at karuizawa without saying a word   i  p pardon me   after mashima cuts him off   karuizawa  please  i m begging you  shut up and listen  i can t concentrate when you prattle on   you two are idiots  i ll explain it later  so don t keep bothering mashima sensei   shooting down karuizawa and the professor   seemed like he wanted to cozy up to school officials    the narration s read on why he polices the others  questions  the main target of his exasperation  the teacher he stammers an apology to","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–46<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Spends the briefing trading barbs with Karuizawa and absorbing Mashima’s rebuke.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I… P-pardon me.” (after Mashima cuts him off)<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Karuizawa, please. I’m begging you, shut up and listen. I can’t concentrate when you prattle on”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You two are idiots. I’ll explain it later, so don’t keep bothering Mashima-sensei.” (shooting down Karuizawa and the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snorted derisively at Karuizawa without saying a word.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “seemed like he wanted to cozy up to school officials” — the narration’s read on why he polices the others’ questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The main target of his exasperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The teacher he stammers an apology to.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the seat and the roll call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  2 3  the failed huddle in the room and then the hallway  he probes ayanokoji  pitches a three man plan  and watches it dissolve   hey  ayanokouji  you ve been quiet  do you actually understand everything   for crying out loud  why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   said once in the room   why on earth was i lumped in with a bunch of space cadets   repeated in the hallway  word for word   i hate to say this  but if we have to be in the same group  we need to put up a unified front  a lot of things will depend on who the vip is  but for now  the four of us should discuss things   h hey  karuizawa  are you listening   maybe in the morning there ll be a notification that one of us was chosen as the vip  if one of us is chosen  it d be smart not to spread it around carelessly  we don t know who might be listening  let s get to a secure location before sharing info   to be honest  i really hate it  no matter what i do  she ll only drag us down   on karuizawa   karuizawa may be gone  but i want to talk about tomorrow  it makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us  let s go  sighs and shakes it off when the professor declines and ayanokoji doesn t engage    he didn t seem to want to work with me  her phone call kills the huddle  he vents about her afterward  the invitee who bows out for love love alive  probes whether he understood the briefing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.49–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the room and then the hallway: he probes Ayanokōji, pitches a three-man plan, and watches it dissolve.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, Ayanokouji. You’ve been quiet. Do you actually understand everything?”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“For crying out loud, why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (said once in the room)<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why on earth was I lumped in with a bunch of space cadets?” (repeated in the hallway, word for word)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate to say this, but if we have to be in the same group, we need to put up a unified front. A lot of things will depend on who the VIP is, but for now, the four of us should discuss things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “H-hey, Karuizawa. Are you listening?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe in the morning there’ll be a notification that one of us was…chosen as the VIP. If one of us is chosen, it’d be smart not to spread it around carelessly. We don’t know who might be listening. Let’s get to a secure location before sharing info.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50-51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I really hate it. No matter what I do, she’ll only drag us down.” (on Karuizawa)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa may be gone, but I want to talk about tomorrow. It makes sense to discuss it with just the three of us. Let’s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sighs and shakes it off when the Professor declines and Ayanokōji doesn’t engage — “He didn’t seem to want to work with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her phone call kills the huddle; he vents about her afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The invitee who bows out for Love Love Alive.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Probes whether he understood the briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the quarrel at the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  2 4  absent from the room named only as missing  when ayanokoji wakes in the cabin  neither he nor koenji is there  absent from the third deck cabin at 20 30   ayanokoji notes the room holds only himself and hirata","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as missing: when Ayanokōji wakes in the cabin, neither he nor Kōenji is there.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Absent from the third-deck cabin at 20:30 — Ayanokōji notes the room holds only himself and Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the failed huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p53-1\">→ After: Ch.2: named in the smarts check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p53-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 2  named in the smarts check named among the ones who have been thinking about the exam  a reply in the hallway says he hasn t been thinking about the exam the way hirata  horikita  and yukimura have   and that he isn t smart either","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: named in the smarts check<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named among the ones who have been thinking about the exam.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A reply in the hallway says he hasn’t been thinking about the exam the way Hirata, Horikita, and Yukimura have — and that he isn’t smart either.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: absent from the room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p65-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p65-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  the grade theory name check named in horikita s score grouping hypothesis  horikita s grade theory  yukimura kun has high academic ability  and so does kouenji kun   they re at the top of the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.65<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Horikita’s score-grouping hypothesis.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita’s grade theory: Yukimura-kun has high academic ability, and so does Kouenji-kun — they’re at the top of the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p53-1\">← Before: Ch.2: named in the smarts check<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"machida-kouji ichinose-honami sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  3 1  from the convenient plan to ichinose storms off the professor s dialect bit  briefs the room hard  then swings through the rabbit discussion   convenient plan first  ichinose s downside last   stop talking like that  it s weird  said yukimura   whatever  i don t care  just talk normal  storms away from the professor s faux archaic provocation  the other two hurry after him   the time for screwing around ended yesterday  from here on out  we need to fight for ourselves and for our classes  yukimura directed that statement toward the professor  but i nodded in acknowledgement   there won t be any negatives  you mean   prompted by machida s four outcomes walk   a hidden downside  what in the world could that be  asked yukimura  sounding flustered  it didn t seem he d considered that point yet  face visibly stiffens when ichinose shows the class a always proposes this pattern    like he wondered how he could have missed such a simple thing   i agree  we can t allow class a to keep securing the lead  added yukimura   i can t trust you  muttered yukimura   rejecting ichinose s alliance offer  the swing of the half  votes with the convenient class a plan  flinches at the hidden downside  then refuses ichinose anyway   he wanted to avoid class d getting the short end and could not commit to trust  first the class a plan s beneficiary  then its questioner  flips to her side on the class gap point  then rejects her alliance on trust  the dialect sparring partner  they walk into rabbit together  hallway companion  one of the names machida uses to teach the outcomes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Storms off the Professor’s dialect bit, briefs the room hard, then swings through the Rabbit discussion — convenient plan first, Ichinose’s downside last.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Stop talking like that. It’s weird,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Whatever, I don’t care. Just talk normal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The time for screwing around ended yesterday. From here on out, we need to fight for ourselves and for our classes.” Yukimura directed that statement toward the Professor, but I nodded in acknowledgement.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Storms away from the Professor’s faux-archaic provocation; the other two hurry after him.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There won’t be any negatives, you mean?” (prompted by Machida’s four-outcomes walk)<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A hidden downside? What in the world could that be?” asked Yukimura, sounding flustered. It didn’t seem he’d considered that point yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Face visibly stiffens when Ichinose shows the Class A always-proposes-this pattern — “like he wondered how he could have missed such a simple thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree. We can’t allow Class A to keep securing the lead,” added Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t trust you,” muttered Yukimura. (rejecting Ichinose’s alliance offer)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The swing of the half: votes with the convenient Class A plan, flinches at the hidden downside, then refuses Ichinose anyway — he wanted to avoid Class D getting the short end and could not commit to trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> First the Class A plan’s beneficiary, then its questioner.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Flips to her side on the class-gap point, then rejects her alliance on trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The dialect sparring partner; they walk into Rabbit together.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Hallway companion; one of the names Machida uses to teach the outcomes.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p65-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the grade-theory name-check<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  3 2 3 5  strategy talk and the kouenji explosion eager to start the class d strategy huddle after the first discussion  back for the second gathering and the cabin when kouenji ends the monkey group   she s always acting strangely  he replied   on karuizawa  the straightforward answer ayanokoji did not want   i don t think we need a breakthrough right now  but we do need a discussion  class a might be breaking away from this test  but i think we need to pinpoint the vip  said yukimura  his words  helped motivate us somewhat  ayanokoji then wonders if he is the target using camouflage   i understand  karuizawa san  but doesn t that just depend on your point of view  i mean  the test on the island was also a surprise to the students  said yukimura  misses the  surprise sunrise  collision with the professor entirely   so you can t trust us  hirata  if you know  then i have the right to know  too  besides  if you know who a vip is  that might give us some kind of hint  we should all be sharing information with each other in the first place  it s only natural  after all  said yukimura   i see  murmured yukimura  he was careful not to say too much   after the two vip names   speaking of rabbit group  it s equally possible for the vip to be from any of the four classes  so in class d  there are two vips that we know about  there should be one more vip keeping his or her identity secret  said yukimura  bolts out of his chair at kouenji s humming   kouenji  stop the happy go lucky act already  i m not going to tell you to take things seriously  but you need to at least participate  we don t want you to screw everything up like you did back on the island  he shouted   you just faked being ill to get out of it   troublesome  you re not even thinking about this test at all  countered yukimura   what did you just do  kouenji  shouted yukimura   the school notification   y you ve got to be kidding me  we re desperately trying to think of a way out of this  and that guy  he just   you re being way too generous  that guy will screw anyone over  so long as he s able to enjoy himself and take it easy  this sucks  shouted yukimura   to hirata s restraint   damn it  thanks to kouenji  things have escalated  said yukimura  the target of every shout in the cabin  pushed for the vip names  then called too generous on kouenji  strategy partner and cabin witness  his flat read on her mood","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.96–97, p.107, p.112–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Eager to start the Class D strategy huddle after the first discussion; back for the second gathering and the cabin when Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“She’s always acting strangely,” he replied. (on Karuizawa; the straightforward answer Ayanokōji did not want)<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t think we need a breakthrough right now, but we do need a discussion. Class A might be breaking away from this test, but I think we need to pinpoint the VIP,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand, Karuizawa-san. But doesn’t that just depend on your point of view? I mean, the test on the island was also a surprise to the students,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His words “helped motivate us somewhat”; Ayanokōji then wonders if he is the target using camouflage.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Misses the “surprise”/“Sunrise” collision with the Professor entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you can’t trust us, Hirata? If you know, then I have the right to know, too. Besides, if you know who a VIP is, that might give us some kind of hint. We should all be sharing information with each other in the first place. It’s only natural, after all,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see,” murmured Yukimura. He was careful not to say too much. (after the two VIP names)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Speaking of Rabbit Group, it’s equally possible for the VIP to be from any of the four classes. So in Class D, there are two VIPs that we know about. There should be one more VIP keeping his or her identity secret,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Bolts out of his chair at Kouenji’s humming: “Kouenji, stop the happy-go-lucky act already! I’m not going to tell you to take things seriously, but you need to at least participate. We don’t want you to screw everything up like you did back on the island,” he shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just faked being ill to get out of it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Troublesome? You’re not even thinking about this test at all!” countered Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What did you just do, Kouenji?!” shouted Yukimura. (the school notification)<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-you’ve got to be kidding me! We’re desperately trying to think of a way out of this, and that guy, he just…”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re being way too generous! That guy will screw anyone over, so long as he’s able to enjoy himself and take it easy. This sucks!” shouted Yukimura. (to Hirata’s restraint)<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn it. Thanks to Kouenji, things have escalated,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The target of every shout in the cabin.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pushed for the VIP names, then called too generous on Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Strategy partner and cabin witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.97, 112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His flat read on her mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: from the convenient plan to Ichinose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3: one of Ichinose’s two props<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p108-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  one of ichinose s two props named with karuizawa as the pair ichinose uses to collect information  by using yukimura and karuizawa  ichinose had started collecting information   the only problem left is when machida notices her ploy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: one of Ichinose’s two props<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.108<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Karuizawa as the pair Ichinose uses to collect information.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> By using Yukimura and Karuizawa, Ichinose had started collecting information — the only problem left is when Machida notices her ploy.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p96-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2–§3.5: strategy talk and the Kouenji explosion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the readable half of the pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p126-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 4  the readable half of the pair named as the group member ayanokoji expects to be able to read  he should be able to find out whatever he needs about the professor and yukimura   the loss is karuizawa alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the readable half of the pair<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.126<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the group member Ayanokōji expects to be able to read.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He should be able to find out whatever he needs about the Professor and Yukimura — the loss is Karuizawa alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3: one of Ichinose’s two props<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the roommate’s VIP probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 4  4 0  the roommate s vip probe alone in the room looking grave  he rants about the group draw rumor  then runs the mutual vip denial with ayanokoji   for crying out loud  why did we get stuck with this group  why am i partnered with karuizawa and sotomura  we can t win  he mumbled   didn t you hear  there s a rumor going around saying that they use guidelines to create the groups  when i heard that all the superior students got grouped into the dragon group  i knew it was true  he answered  treats the dragon  best of the best  roster as proof the draw was fixed  dissatisfied at rabbit s middle placement  academic ability not inferior to hirata or horikita  narration   ayanokouji  you aren t the vip  are you  he asked   cooperation is vital in this test  we need to adhere to that  if we cooperate  we won t lose   are you sure  you re not being selfish and trying to hoard points  are you   yes  of course you can  i m not the vip  neither is sotomura  by the way  vouches sotomura is not the vip without being asked for proof  reports her vip denial and adds he may not believe it   disdain as the standing attitude  doubts everyone as a rule  satisfied for the time being and settles into sighs while ayanokoji naps","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the roommate’s VIP probe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.131–133<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Alone in the room looking grave; he rants about the group-draw rumor, then runs the mutual VIP denial with Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“For crying out loud, why did we get stuck with this group? Why am I partnered with Karuizawa and Sotomura? We can’t win,” he mumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Didn’t you hear? There’s a rumor going around saying that they use guidelines to create the groups. When I heard that all the superior students got grouped into the Dragon group, I knew it was true,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji. You aren’t the VIP, are you?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Treats the Dragon “best of the best” roster as proof the draw was fixed; dissatisfied at Rabbit’s middle placement; academic ability not inferior to Hirata or Horikita (narration).<span class=\"pg\">p.131-132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cooperation is vital in this test. We need to adhere to that. If we cooperate, we won’t lose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure? You’re not being selfish and trying to hoard points, are you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, of course you can. I’m not the VIP. Neither is Sotomura, by the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Vouches Sotomura is not the VIP without being asked for proof.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Reports her VIP denial and adds he may not believe it — disdain as the standing attitude.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doubts everyone as a rule; satisfied for the time being and settles into sighs while Ayanokōji naps.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the readable half of the pair<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p136-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the alibi chain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p136-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 4  the alibi chain named in the room s round of vip checks   cleared twice without being asked  karuizawa reports that it seems yukimura kun and that soto kun aren t the vip  ayanokoji notes yukimura had asked him the same question a little while ago  ayanokoji states with certainty that neither he nor yukimura is the vip  and leaves the yukimura sourced clear of karuizawa and the professor unsaid  convinced yukimura isn t the vip either  the four cleared leave ten suspects remaining","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p136-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the alibi chain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.136, p.152–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the room’s round of VIP checks — cleared twice without being asked.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa reports that it seems Yukimura-kun and that Soto…kun aren’t the VIP; Ayanokōji notes Yukimura had asked him the same question a little while ago.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji states with certainty that neither he nor Yukimura is the VIP, and leaves the Yukimura-sourced clear of Karuizawa and the Professor unsaid.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Convinced Yukimura isn’t the VIP either, the four cleared leave ten suspects remaining.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the roommate’s VIP probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 4  4 2  the stairwell sits near ayanokoji in the evening room  mutters the vip worry  then follows the class c trio into the emergency stairwell and breaks the corner with a shout   this isn t good   yeah  if things continue like this  the vip will get away   yukimura  next to ayanokoji  spots the three girls on her tail  grumbles she always makes people hate her  throws the stairwell door open  tries to check on her  gets slapped away  and leaves exhausted   hey  did you get a weird vibe from those three just now  asked yukimura   you think they have a bone to pick with her  asked yukimura   let s follow them  i don t think there ll be violence  but it could lead to an uproar   damn karuizawa  she s always making people hate her  i wanted us to spend our precious time finding the vip  yukimura grumbled   what are you doing  yukimura shouted   don t you think it s better to just let things go  they bumped into   each other  it s not like karuizawa was at fault  yukimura said  glared into silence by the trio under their weight   falls silent  then takes karuizawa s  pathetic  look for it   are you okay  asked yukimura  who seemed unable to leave karuizawa to their mercy   hey  what the hell  i only came to check on you because i was worried   jeez  what s with her  she s always  always causing trouble for people  exhausted from the ordeal  leaves without another word   resentment and the failed rescue both in one exit  the professor s pompous  i can t say that i noticed anything of the sort  answer next to him   yukimura s vibe read called right on the money by narration","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.155–165<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits near Ayanokōji in the evening room, mutters the VIP worry, then follows the Class C trio into the emergency stairwell and breaks the corner with a shout.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“This isn’t good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. If things continue like this, the VIP will get away.” (Yukimura, next to Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey. Did you get a weird vibe from those three just now?” asked Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Spots the three girls on her tail, grumbles she always makes people hate her, throws the stairwell door open, tries to check on her, gets slapped away, and leaves exhausted.<span class=\"pg\">p.159-165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You think they have a bone to pick with her?” asked Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s follow them. I don’t think there’ll be violence, but it could lead to an uproar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn Karuizawa. She’s always making people hate her. I wanted us to spend our precious time finding the VIP,” Yukimura grumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you doing?!” Yukimura shouted.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think it’s better to just let things go? They bumped into … each other. It’s not like Karuizawa was at fault,” Yukimura said.<span class=\"pg\">p.163-164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Glared into silence by the trio under their weight — falls silent, then takes Karuizawa’s “pathetic” look for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.163-164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay?” asked Yukimura, who seemed unable to leave Karuizawa to their mercy.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, what the hell? I only came to check on you because I was worried!”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jeez, what’s with her? She’s always, always causing trouble for people!”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Exhausted from the ordeal, leaves without another word — resentment and the failed rescue both in one exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The Professor’s pompous “I can’t say that I noticed anything of the sort” answer next to him — Yukimura’s vibe read called right on the money by narration.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p136-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the alibi chain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p173-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the fight corroborated<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p173-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 4  the fight corroborated named as the second witness to the manabe attack  asked whether she saw it  karuizawa answers that she did   and that yukimura saw it  too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p173-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the fight corroborated<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.173<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the second witness to the Manabe attack.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked whether she saw it, Karuizawa answers that she did — and that Yukimura saw it, too.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p155-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2: the stairwell<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the VIP steps forward<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio machida-kouji sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 5  5 0 5 2  the vip steps forward melancholy at the card table  the self reliance rebuke  then under the email show pressure he demands phones on the table and reveals himself as the rabbit vip   after ayanokoji s secret swap   is it okay to just sit here like this  yukimura sighed   no thanks  i don t really feel like it  really  is this okay  ichinose san  i mean  just doing this until the test ends  i thought you were the one leading the group here   yeah  good point  he answered  knows he can t take the leadership thrust on him but still wants a way to change things  academic top   natural leader  narration  the downer at her table  takes the  rely on yourself  rebuke   yukimura dono  and the professor s joint barrage  tries to stop the show  then  i m sorry for lying to you  ayanokouji   all alone with ichinose dono  my word  how suspicious  a clandestine rendezvous  wouldn t you say   professor s line  in exchange   wait  ayanokouji  there s no way this kind of strategy is going to work  said yukimura   wait  it s not just ayanokouji kun  you re going along with this  karuizawa  you agree with this  yukimura was puzzled   do you really think that   showing everyone your phone is the right move  he asked   to the professor  yukimura s expression stiffened   ibuki s vip jibe  her  you re not the vip  are you  freezes him   the jibe that starts the class a stare   before i do so  i want you to promise me one thing  he said   i don t want anyone here to turn traitor  especially you  class a  i want you to take out your phones and put them in front of you  that goes for everybody  everyone  put your phones where i can see them  he demanded   exactly what i said  nothing more  nothing less   i m sorry for lying to you  ayanokouji  he muttered   i m the vip  watches the private email and chat logs  confirms authenticity for the room   wha  y yukimura dono  you re the vip  the professor stammers  her genuine shock is the cover for the swap   class d s surprise sells the lie  the vip email on screen  class d s 500 000 given up in the room   but the phones were already exchanged in secret   if i d known things would turn out like this  i would ve talked from the start    the regret that makes the reveal human","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the VIP steps forward<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Melancholy at the card table, the self-reliance rebuke, then under the email-show pressure he demands phones on the table and reveals himself as the Rabbit VIP — after Ayanokōji’s secret swap.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is it okay to just sit here like this?” Yukimura sighed.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No thanks. I don’t really feel like it. Really, is this okay, Ichinose-san? I mean, just doing this until the test ends. I thought you were the one leading the group here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. Good point,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Knows he can’t take the leadership thrust on him but still wants a way to change things; academic top ≠ natural leader (narration).<span class=\"pg\">p.205-206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The downer at her table; takes the “rely on yourself” rebuke.<span class=\"pg\">p.205-206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yukimura-dono” and the Professor’s joint barrage; tries to stop the show; then “I’m sorry for lying to you, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.217, 220, 223-224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All alone with Ichinose-dono? My word, how suspicious. A clandestine rendezvous, wouldn’t you say?” (Professor’s line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ayanokouji. There’s no way this kind of strategy is going to work,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. It’s not just Ayanokouji-kun? You’re going along with this, Karuizawa? You agree with this?” Yukimura was puzzled.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you really think that … showing everyone your phone is the right move?” he asked. (to the Professor)<span class=\"pg\">p.222-223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Yukimura’s expression stiffened. (Ibuki’s VIP jibe)<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Her “You’re not the VIP, are you?” freezes him — the jibe that starts the Class A stare.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before I do so, I want you to promise me one thing,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t want anyone here to turn traitor. Especially you, Class A. I want you to take out your phones and put them in front of you. That goes for everybody. Everyone, put your phones where I can see them,” he demanded.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly what I said. Nothing more, nothing less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry for lying to you, Ayanokouji,” he muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Watches the private email and chat logs; confirms authenticity for the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> “Wha— Y-Yukimura-dono, you’re the VIP?!” the Professor stammers.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Her genuine shock is the cover for the swap — Class D’s surprise sells the lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The VIP email on screen; Class D’s 500,000 given up in the room — but the phones were already exchanged in secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “If I’d known things would turn out like this, I would’ve talked from the start…” — the regret that makes the reveal human.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p173-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the fight corroborated<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the cover holds, then cracks<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami machida-kouji yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 5  5 2  the cover holds  then cracks accepts the blame as the points grabber  begs every class to trust outcome  1  and rages when ichinose s call exposes the swap    too bad  from machida is the last he hears before the room empties   no  it s okay  it s probably for the best  i thought i could lie my way out of this  but i was wrong  i m sure you  sotomura  and karuizawa would agree this was for the best  said yukimura  named in the trio who all agree the reveal was for the best  same trio   the real vip he still does not know about   well  now everyone knows the answer  it s me  yukimura said  everyone now pictures him hoarding points for himself   the role he agreed to play   i want to believe  no  i do believe in everyone  yukimura begged fervently  the joy at winning the cover dies the moment the phone vibrates  he lunges  drops it face up  caller id  ichinose   damn it  shouted yukimura   i was wrong to go along with your plan  this sucks  he fumed  her call is what breaks him  machida s  too bad  yukimura  piles on the mockery  the mockery line after the drop   class a laughs at the failed gambit  leaves the room visibly upset and shaking  the vip cover traded for a public traitor face","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: the cover holds, then cracks<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–228<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Accepts the blame as the points-grabber, begs every class to trust Outcome #1, and rages when Ichinose’s call exposes the swap — “Too bad” from Machida is the last he hears before the room empties.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, it’s okay. It’s probably for the best. I thought I could lie my way out of this, but I was wrong. I’m sure you, Sotomura, and Karuizawa would agree this was for the best,” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, now everyone knows the answer. It’s me,” Yukimura said.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to believe… No, I do believe in everyone.” Yukimura begged fervently.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Named in the trio who all agree the reveal was for the best.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Same trio — the real VIP he still does not know about.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Everyone now pictures him hoarding points for himself — the role he agreed to play.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The joy at winning the cover dies the moment the phone vibrates; he lunges, drops it face-up, caller ID “Ichinose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226-228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn it!” shouted Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was wrong to go along with your plan. This sucks,” he fumed.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her call is what breaks him; Machida’s “Too bad, Yukimura” piles on the mockery.<span class=\"pg\">p.225-228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The mockery line after the drop — Class A laughs at the failed gambit.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Leaves the room visibly upset and shaking; the VIP cover traded for a public traitor face.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0–5.2: the VIP steps forward<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p230-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the truth he never had<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p230-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 5  the truth he never had named in ichinose s reconstruction of how the reveal was engineered  after a falsehood comes to light  most people take the answer after it as the truth   yukimura kun was determined not to be the one who blinks  ichinose saw through the plan behind the plan  including the truth kept hidden even from yukimura  ayanokoji approached him under the pretense of being the vip  asked why she thought it was karuizawa  the answer cites the same reason as yukimura kun   her unusually changed behavior","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p230-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the truth he never had<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.230–232<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Ichinose’s reconstruction of how the reveal was engineered.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After a falsehood comes to light, most people take the answer after it as the truth — Yukimura-kun was determined not to be the one who blinks.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose saw through the plan behind the plan, including the truth kept hidden even from Yukimura: Ayanokōji approached him under the pretense of being the VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked why she thought it was Karuizawa, the answer cites the same reason as Yukimura-kun — her unusually changed behavior.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v4-p225-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2: the cover holds, then cracks<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action","w":"hirata-yousuke hondou-ryoutaro ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  3  hands  votes and the roster yukimura is named among the students who follow sudou into horikita s camp  and he later handles the grip strength device and makes the scavenger hunt roster  raises his hand with sudou and sakura for horikita s ability plan  takes his turn at the grip strength meter after sudou s 82 4  is handed a grip strength device by hirata  alongside hondou  picked with ayanokoji  sotomura  mori and maezono for the scavenger hunt   ayanokouji kun  yukimura kun  sotomura kun  mori san  and maezono san","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3: Hands, votes and the roster<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura is named among the students who follow Sudou into Horikita’s camp, and he later handles the grip-strength device and makes the scavenger-hunt roster.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#hondou-ryoutaro\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Raises his hand with Sudou and Sakura for Horikita’s ability plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes his turn at the grip-strength meter after Sudou’s 82.4.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> Is handed a grip-strength device by Hirata, alongside Hondou.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Picked with Ayanokōji, Sotomura, Mori and Maezono for the scavenger hunt: “Ayanokouji-kun, Yukimura-kun, Sotomura-kun, Mori-san, and Maezono-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: seventh and seventh<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 6  6  seventh and seventh yukimura grumbles back to camp after a second straight seventh place  downtrodden before the hurdles and flag   seventh and seventh  he grumbled  gets space rather than comfort  then a redirect to the written tests he still plans to ace   i won t fail  but my scores will plummet  said yukimura  wants class a more than anyone  so the burden of a bad sports day sits heavier on him than on most  brings up the rear of the capture the flag offense with ike and ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: seventh and seventh<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.98–101<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura grumbles back to camp after a second straight seventh place, downtrodden before the hurdles and flag.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Seventh and seventh,” he grumbled.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I won’t fail, but my scores will plummet.” said Yukimura.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets space rather than comfort, then a redirect to the written tests he still plans to ace.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wants Class A more than anyone, so the burden of a bad sports day sits heavier on him than on most.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Brings up the rear of the capture-the-flag offense with Ike and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3: Hands, votes and the roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: cutting the leader<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 6  6  cutting the leader yukimura interjects while sudou demands the class follow him after the cavalry loss   is that really the case   it seems like you just want to show off how amazing you are   your emotions are completely out of control  and they re making all your decisions for you  cuts sudou s  trying my hardest for the class  claim  sudou tells him to shut up  then punches hirata instead  the academic who resents sudou s sports day power finally says the quiet part aloud   and nearly becomes the fist s target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: cutting the leader<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.132<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yukimura interjects while Sudou demands the class follow him after the cavalry loss.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is that really the case?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It seems like you just want to show off how amazing you are.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Your emotions are completely out of control, and they’re making all your decisions for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Cuts Sudou’s “trying my hardest for the class” claim; Sudou tells him to shut up, then punches Hirata instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The academic who resents Sudou’s sports-day power finally says the quiet part aloud — and nearly becomes the fist’s target.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: seventh and seventh<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p133-1\">→ After: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p133-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 6  a passing mention named as the classmate sudou looked ready to punch after the cavalry battles  he looked on the verge of punching yukimura anyway  hitting hirata earned sudou everyone s attention instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p133-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.133<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the classmate Sudou looked ready to punch after the cavalry battles.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He looked on the verge of punching Yukimura anyway; hitting Hirata earned Sudou everyone’s attention instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v5-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: cutting the leader<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p36-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 3  excellent but partner dependent named with horikita as an excellent student who could still be at risk depending on who the short test pairs them with  same risk class  top grades are not safe if the partner is weak  no dialogue or action from yukimura on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p36-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: excellent but partner-dependent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.36<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Horikita as an excellent student who could still be at risk depending on who the short test pairs them with.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Same risk class: top grades are not safe if the partner is weak.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue or action from Yukimura on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.4: photo witness and pawn candidate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p73-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"manabe-shiho ayanokouji-kiyotaka ishizaki-daichi kaneda-satoru ryuuen-kakeru yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 4  photo witness and pawn candidate named with ayanokouji as the class d students who saw manabe s group bullying karuizawa  manabe s testimony places him at the cruise ship incident  photo taken after  later deleted  the other photo name  both dismissed as mere pawns by ryuuen after the debate  ishizaki  yukimura does look a little suspicious  he seems pretty smart kaneda  either yukimura shi or ayanokouji shi took the picture  the facts state that only yukimura or ayanokouji could have taken that picture   then both possibly pawns  yukimura does not appear in person on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: photo witness and pawn candidate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.73–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Ayanokouji as the Class D students who saw Manabe’s group bullying Karuizawa.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Manabe’s testimony places him at the cruise-ship incident; photo taken after, later deleted.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The other photo name; both dismissed as mere pawns by Ryuuen after the debate.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Ishizaki: Yukimura does look a little suspicious. He seems pretty smart<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Kaneda: either Yukimura-shi or Ayanokouji-shi took the picture.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> the facts state that only Yukimura or Ayanokouji could have taken that picture — then both possibly pawns.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yukimura does not appear in person on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p36-1\">← Before: Ch.3: excellent but partner-dependent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3–5.5: the cavalry who tutors<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p87-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune miyake-akito hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka kaneda-satoru ishizaki-daichi sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 5  5 3 5 5  the cavalry who tutors inserts himself into the horikita hirata ayanokoji talk and offers to tutor miyake and hasebe   in that case  i ll take care of tutoring them   if i don t help out where i can  we won t be able to pass the test   same goes for you  horikita  you can t do everything yourself  there s just one problem  i can teach miyake and hasebe how to study  but i m not friendly with them  after seeing what happened here earlier  i get the feeling that talking to them will be tricky  i was hoping you could do the work of convincing them to study with me  horikita overjoyed  she promises to convince the pair for him  leads the pallet session  marks their sheets  sets a ten question timed drill  plans seven or eight meetings before the final  presses hasebe s abrupt exit  then works her into the same drill  accepts her decision to stay   why would she need to   so  you hate being seen talking to us   excuse me  i d like to say something before we begin   no hiding anything  ayanokouji   studying  horikita says you re quite capable   are you the type to hide his abilities   you should take this study group seriously  then  with me tutoring you  you ll definitely score higher than you did on the midterm   did you bring your answer sheets from the midterm and first semester exams like i asked   both of you excel in the sciences  your humanities scores are a complete disaster   i didn t know you two were so close   so  why did you agree to join us  writing on their papers while class c roars at the cafe counter  unmoved by ishizaki s scene   who knows  doesn t have anything to do with us  open about his own tutoring failure in junior high  why he finally helps  the sports festival and  selfish mother  line of thought   i ve never really taught someone else how to study before  i mean  a long time ago  i taught this one junior high idiot to pull an all nighter  but i couldn t stand it  i wasn t able to concentrate on the material  because he didn t have the fundamentals down   even now  i can t forget the time i wasted  i thought it was so stupid  trying to teach people how to study  when you and horikita rounded up those guys who were about to fail  and held those study sessions  honestly  i was laughing at you  the same goes for hirata s group  i mean  doesn t it seem like a waste  nearly everyone who hates studying just can t study in the first place  i felt like teaching them to cram for a couple days was useless  since they d just go back to how they were before   i was useless in the sports festival  i got tripped up by the thing i dismissed as unimportant  just being able to study isn t enough for this   school  just being athletic isn t enough  if you combine those two things  that still isn t enough  even people like horikita and hirata  who are gifted both academically and athletically  definitely can t make it through the challenges ahead with just those skills alone  intuition  insight  and taste  we have to rely on those traits  which are essential for living in society  working as a team is vital  that s the only way we win   so  i decided to help  also  i was self centered  i thought i d be fine as long as i could study  all i worried about was myself  i was just like my selfish mother  that s why i took a good hard look at myself  and  ah  that s not important  forget it   if i had to tutor ike and the other guys  i d probably have a much worse time of it  miyake and hasebe both take their studies seriously  so it might be easy  besides  they re already good at science  it shouldn t be too hard to cover the rest  i don t know much i ll be able to help  but we ll probably see at least some improvement  predicts kaneda will write class c s questions   the best student in class c  utterance fragment recorded as narrative  yeah   well  the questions might seem impossible for us to imagine right now  but what if we identify the people coming up with them  personally  i think kaneda will do it   i don t know if i d put it like that  but yeah  he s the best student in class c  rejects ryuuen or ishizaki as question writers   no subject mastery  no tricky questions   no way  without a thorough understanding of the subject  they won t be able to come up with anything  take you two  for example  think about subjects you re poor at  like the humanities  do you really think you d be able to create a tricky question   yeah  besides  what kind of social studies problems would even be on the test   exactly  at best  you d think of the most obvious problems  even if you scoured the textbook for the really difficult parts  if you didn t establish the problem properly  the school would probably turn it down  accepts the extreme question probe idea  needs horikita and hirata s help through ayanokoji  short utterance  true   we ll probably need to come up with provisional questions as soon as possible so we can identify the school s standards  i ll try to create questions myself  but would horikita and hirata be willing to help out   you re the only person who can get in touch with them  ayanokouji  utterance fragment recorded as narrative  yeah  okay   well  i m not in any clubs  so i m good  let s decide when to meet based on what works for miyacchi   i thought you were going to back out  hasebe  this is unusual  you don t normally want to get involved in anything   well  i suppose this is enough for today  the first study session is the day after tomorrow  notes sakura still has not come over when they leave","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3–5.5: the cavalry who tutors<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.87–103<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Inserts himself into the Horikita–Hirata–Ayanokōji talk and offers to tutor Miyake and Hasebe.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“In that case, I’ll take care of tutoring them,”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If I don’t help out where I can, we won’t be able to pass the test,”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Same goes for you, Horikita. You can’t do everything yourself. There’s just one problem. I can teach Miyake and Hasebe how to study, but I’m not friendly with them. After seeing what happened here earlier, I get the feeling that…”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Same goes for you, Horikita. You can’t do everything yourself. There’s just one problem. I can teach Miyake and Hasebe how to study, but I’m not friendly with them. After seeing what happened here earlier, I get the feeling that talking to them will be tricky. I was hoping you could do the work of convincing them to study with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita overjoyed; she promises to convince the pair for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Leads the Pallet session; marks their sheets; sets a ten-question timed drill; plans seven or eight meetings before the final.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Presses Hasebe’s abrupt exit, then works her into the same drill; accepts her decision to stay.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why would she need to?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you hate being seen talking to us?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Excuse me? I’d like to say something before we begin,”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No hiding anything, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Studying. Horikita says you’re quite capable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you the type to hide his abilities?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should take this study group seriously, then. With me tutoring you, you’ll definitely score higher than you did on the midterm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you bring your answer sheets from the midterm and first semester exams like I asked?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both of you excel in the sciences. Your humanities scores are a complete disaster,”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t know you two were so close,”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, why did you agree to join us?”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Writing on their papers while Class C roars at the café counter; unmoved by Ishizaki’s scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who knows? Doesn’t have anything to do with us,”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Open about his own tutoring failure in junior high; why he finally helps; the sports festival and “selfish mother” line of thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve never really taught someone else how to study before. I mean, a long time ago, I taught this one junior-high idiot to pull an all-nighter, but I couldn’t stand it. I wasn’t able to concentrate on the material, because he didn’t have the fundamentals down,”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even now, I can’t forget the time I wasted. I thought it was so stupid, trying to teach people how to study. When you and Horikita rounded up those guys who were about to fail, and held those study sessions, honestly, I was laughing at you. The same goes for Hirata’s group. I mean, doesn’t it seem like a waste? Nearly everyone who hates studying just can’t study in the first place. I felt like teaching them to cram for a couple days was useless, since they’d just go back to how they were before.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was useless in the sports festival. I got tripped up by the thing I dismissed as unimportant. Just being able to study isn’t enough for this”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “school. Just being athletic isn’t enough. If you combine those two things, that still isn’t enough. Even people like Horikita and Hirata, who are gifted both academically and athletically, definitely can’t make it through the challenges ahead with just those skills alone. Intuition, insight, and taste. We have to rely on those traits, which are essential for living in society. Working as a team is vital. That’s the only way we win,”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, I decided to help. Also, I was self-centered. I thought I’d be fine as long as I could study. All I worried about was myself. I was just like my selfish mother. That’s why I took a good hard look at myself, and… Ah, that’s not important. Forget it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I had to tutor Ike and the other guys, I’d probably have a much worse time of it. Miyake and Hasebe both take their studies seriously, so it might be easy. Besides, they’re already good at science. It shouldn’t be too hard to cover the rest. I don’t know much I’ll be able to help, but we’ll probably see at least some improvement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Predicts Kaneda will write Class C’s questions — the best student in Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Utterance fragment recorded as narrative: Yeah,<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, the questions might seem impossible for us to imagine right now, but what if we identify the people coming up with them? Personally, I think Kaneda will do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know if I’d put it like that, but yeah. He’s the best student in Class C,”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Rejects Ryuuen or Ishizaki as question-writers — no subject mastery, no tricky questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way. Without a thorough understanding of the subject, they won’t be able to come up with anything. Take you two, for example. Think about subjects you’re poor at, like the humanities. Do you really think you’d be able to create a tricky question?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Besides, what kind of social studies problems would even be on the test?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Exactly. At best, you’d think of the most obvious problems. Even if you scoured the textbook for the really difficult parts, if you didn’t establish the problem properly, the school would probably turn it down,”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Accepts the extreme-question probe idea; needs Horikita and Hirata’s help through Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Short utterance: True,<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll probably need to come up with provisional questions as soon as possible so we can identify the school’s standards. I’ll try to create questions myself, but would Horikita and Hirata be willing to help out?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the only person who can get in touch with them, Ayanokouji,”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Utterance fragment recorded as narrative: Yeah. Okay.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’m not in any clubs, so I’m good. Let’s decide when to meet based on what works for Miyacchi.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought you were going to back out, Hasebe. This is unusual. You don’t normally want to get involved in anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose this is enough for today. The first study session is the day after tomorrow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Notes Sakura still has not come over when they leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p73-1\">← Before: Ch.4: photo witness and pawn candidate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p104-1\">→ After: Ch.5: named in the management lecture<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p104-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune yukimura-teruhiko","q":"yukimura teruhiko ch 5  named in the management lecture named as not yet accustomed to tutoring while horikita lists the session problems  his  horikita s and hirata s questions form the fundamental basis  more helpers raise leak risk  no dialogue from yukimura on these pages  present only in the dorm call analysis","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p104-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: named in the management lecture<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.104–105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as not yet accustomed to tutoring while Horikita lists the session problems.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> His, Horikita’s and Hirata’s questions form the fundamental basis; more helpers raise leak risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No dialogue from Yukimura on these pages; present only in the dorm-call analysis.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v6-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.3–5.5: the cavalry who tutors<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
